      "name": "Combined Move-and-Store Operations",
      "description": "Combined move-and-store operations: a move with a storage interval between move-out and move-in, run as one coordinated plan — survey, quote, pack, load, intake, hold, redelivery, placement, reassembly, unpacking, and a final walkthrough. The move side is the published residential pattern: whole-home and apartment moves of every size; loading, transport and unloading; furniture protection and careful placement; disassembly and reassembly of standard furniture, planned up front; full, partial, or fragile-only packing plus unpacking at the other end; white-glove care for antiques and high-value pieces; custom crates when a piece needs more than padding. Where a move includes a high-mass asset of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs, that piece moves under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation with L/360 floor-deflection analysis, as part of the same flat-rate move. The hold side, on the company's confirmed terms: items are held in leased storage between move-out and move-in, for any type of items — including containers, household goods, and machines such as robotic arms — with a 30-day minimum stay; customers can access their stored items while stored; lease terms vary; then goods are redelivered and placed room by room when the destination is ready. The quote path: one flat price in writing before move day for the job, through Get My Flat Rate Quote — the Short (Quick Quote) form by default or the Detailed Project form, switching in place with From, To and What's moving preserved — or the free film-only video walkthrough survey room, where the customer films and a person makes the estimate; nothing is auto-priced. Domain facts, labeled as such: a mover-held gap move typically involves two handlings against four for a self-storage gap; the condition recorded at intake is mirrored at release; redelivery is triggered by destination readiness, not by the calendar alone.",
